.TH RUFUS 1 "November 2026" "Rufus" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rufus \- The Reliable USB Formatting Utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rufus
[\fB\-x\fR] [\fB\-h\fR] [\fB\-f\fR \fIFILESYSTEM\fR] [\fB\-i\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-l\fR \fILOCALE\fR] [\fB\-w\fR \fITIMEOUT\fR] [\fIIMAGE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rufus is a utility that helps format and create bootable USB flash drives,
from ISO images (Windows, Linux, etc.), disk images (including compressed ones),
FreeDOS, MS-DOS, Syslinux or GRUB. It requires administrative privileges and
is started through \fBpkexec\fR(1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-extra\-devs\fR
List extra devices, such as USB hard drives.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR \fIPATH\fR, \fB\-\-iso\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Select the image pointed by \fIPATH\fR on startup.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR \fILOCALE\fR, \fB\-\-locale\fR=\fILOCALE\fR
Select the locale to use (e.g. tr\-TR).
.TP
\fB\-f\fR \fIFILESYSTEM\fR, \fB\-\-filesystem\fR=\fIFILESYSTEM\fR
Preselect the file system to use.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR \fITIMEOUT\fR, \fB\-\-wait\fR=\fITIMEOUT\fR
Wait \fITIMEOUT\fR tenths of seconds for another instance to exit.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display the usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/rufus/rufus.ini\fR
User settings.
.TP
\fI/var/cache/rufus\fR
Downloaded (signature verified) bootloader files and the log of the last session.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://rufus.ie
